# Standalone mongot @VERSION@ prerelease

Source commit: `@COMMIT@`. Server platform: **Linux x86_64**. Client packages are platform independent.
Download the assets from this GitHub release and keep SHA256SUMS alongside them:

```sh
sha256sum --ignore-missing -c SHA256SUMS
```

## Server

```sh
tar -xzf mongot-standalone-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tgz
cd mongot-standalone
./mongot-standalone --config standalone.yaml
```

The archive includes Java 21, native libraries, licenses and the API schema. The sample
configuration binds unauthenticated loopback port 27029 and persists to ./data. SIGTERM stops it.
Secure external listeners with TLS and collection/role-scoped bearer principals as described in
[the operating guide](https://github.com/beardsandbeers/mongot/blob/@COMMIT@/docs/standalone-mongot.md).

## Client packages

- **Python 3.10+**: `python -m pip install mongot_standalone_client-@VERSION@-py3-none-any.whl`.
  The `.tar.gz` is the source distribution; pip can install it instead.
- **Node 22+/TypeScript**: `npm install ./mongot-standalone-client-@VERSION@.tgz`.
  Use `require('@mongot/standalone-client')` or import the typed package. Compiled JS, declarations
  and the schema are included.
- **Java 17+**: unzip `mongot-standalone-client-java-@VERSION@.zip`. Its main JAR bundles runtime
  dependencies, exposes the typed library, and runs as a JSON-lines adapter with `java -jar`.
- **Rust**: extract `mongot-standalone-client-@VERSION@.crate` with tar and add a Cargo path dependency
  on the resulting directory. A current stable Rust compiler and crates.io access are required.
  The crate includes the protobuf schema and a vendored protoc build dependency. Cargo verifies
  that it builds independently of this repository.

Python, npm and Cargo resolve dependencies through their normal registries. The Java main JAR
bundles its dependencies. These assets are uploaded to this repository; they are not published
to language package registries.

[Full API examples](https://github.com/beardsandbeers/mongot/blob/@COMMIT@/clients/README.md).
All clients expose the 16 catalog/document/query/status RPCs, BSON helpers, TLS/bearer auth and
per-call deadlines. Preserve request IDs/payloads for retries and inspect per-item write outcomes.

## Verification and provenance

The manifest records the source commit, platform, artifact sizes and SHA-256 hashes. Packaged-client
verification reports exercise every RPC, index/document changes and process restart using clients
installed from these assets. Confirm `passed: true` in the reports.
